# Strip Mine may target itself (it is a land when the ability is announced). The cost, tapping and sacrificing it, is paid
# first (CR 602.2b), so the target is gone when the ability resolves and it does nothing (CR 608.2b): Bot1's Forest and
# Bot2's Island are untouched. Strip Mine is in its owner's graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Strip Mine
Forest
Forest x5
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Island x6
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Strip Mine.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Strip Mine.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Strip Mine)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Strip Mine
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest
Bot2.Battlefield = Island
